{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART trap `TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xe9 want 0xa5` with tohost FAIL 0xdead. Root cause at picosoc/simpleuart.v:126 (excerpt line 126) loads `send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b1}` so start-bit is 1 not 0; receiver misses true start and re-frames on first zero of 0xa5 shifting it to 0xe9. Fixing start-bit to 0 restores 10-bit start+data+stop framing driven via picosoc/picosoc.v:201 reg_dat_we path.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@
 			end else
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
-				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b1};
+				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0};
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP uart mismatch, loopback 0xa5 received correctly"}

